      },
      {
        "slide_number": 2,
        "title": "The Problem",
        "points": [
          "**Social Anxiety:** 66% of adults feel negative about tipping, often driven by the fear of social judgment.",
          "**Inconsistency:** A 20% tip at a dive bar means something different than a 20% tip at a Michelin-star venue.",
          "**Lack of Transparency:** Diners rarely know if a 'Service Charge' actually goes to the staff or the house.",
          "**Travel Confusion:** Tourists are often baffled by local tipping customs, leading to awkward interactions."
        ]
      },
      {
        "slide_number": 3,
        "title": "The Solution: Tipperary",
        "content": "Tipperary is the 'Glassdoor for Tipping.' It is a mobile app that crowdsources gratuity data to provide transparency for diners.",
        "key_features": [
          "**Venue-Specific Averages:** Search any restaurant to see the average tip percentage left by previous diners over the last 30 days.",
          "**Service-Based Benchmarks:** See average tips categorized by service quality (e.g., 'Standard Service: 18%', 'Exceptional Service: 22%').",
          "**Policy Transparency:** User-flagged data on whether the venue adds automatic gratuity or administrative fees."
        ]
      },
      {
        "slide_number": 4,
        "title": "How It Works",
        "steps": [
          "1. **Check-In:** The user opens Tipperary at the restaurant.",
          "2. **View Data:** The app displays the 'Tipperary Norm'—the median tip percentage for that specific location.",
          "3. **Contribute:** After paying, the user anonymously logs their bill total and tip amount (or scans their receipt).",
          "4. **Earn:** Users earn points for data contribution, redeemable for discounts at partner venues."
        ]
      },
      {
        "slide_number": 5,
        "title": "Market Opportunity",
        "market_segments": [
          "**The Anxious Diner:** Millennials and Gen Z who value financial transparency and social norms.",
          "**The Business Traveler:** Professionals expensing meals who need to justify tip amounts to accounting departments.",
          "**International Tourists:** Visitors navigating the complex US tipping culture."
        ],
        "total_addressable_market": "The US Full Service Restaurant market is valued at over $289 Billion. Tipping is an integral transaction layer on top of nearly every meal."
      },
      {
        "slide_number": 6,
        "title": "Business Model",
        "revenue_streams": [
          {
            "stream": "B2B Data Intelligence (Primary)",
            "description": "Selling aggregated, anonymized data to hospitality groups and market researchers to benchmark staff performance and wage competitiveness."
          },
          {
            "stream": "Hyper-Local Advertising",
            "description": "Restaurants can pay to promote 'Happy Hour' specials to users currently looking up tip rates in the immediate vicinity."
          },
          {
            "stream": "Premium User Tier",
            "description": "Ad-free experience with advanced analytics for power users (e.g., expense reporting integration)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "slide_number": 7,
        "title": "Competitive Advantage",
        "differentiation": "While Yelp and Google Reviews focus on food quality and ambiance, they lack granular financial data regarding gratuity. Tipperary owns the 'Post-Meal, Pre-Payment' niche, a high-intent moment that current competitors ignore."
      },
      {
        "slide_number": 8,
        "title": "The Ask",
        "request": "We are seeking $500k in Pre-Seed funding to develop the MVP, acquire our first 10,000 users in three major metro test markets (NYC, LA, Chicago), and secure initial data partnerships."
      }
    ]
  }
}
